1. You MAY (free, no permission needed)
   a. Download, install, and use this app / code for PERSONAL,
      non-commercial purposes (including for WhatsApp groups / channels you
      run yourself, as long as nobody is charged for it).
   b. Read, study, and audit the source code.
   c. Modify the code for your own use, as long as the result is NOT
      distributed.
   d. Fork on GitHub SOLELY to submit improvements (pull requests) to the
      original repository, or to keep a private copy.
   e. Write and share your own bot scripts (plugins) that use this app's
      script API — those scripts are yours.

2. You may NOT, without prior written permission from the copyright holder
   a. Sell, rent, or charge for this app, this code, or any derivative in any
      form (including "bot setup services", rented bots, or subscriptions).
   b. Redistribute the APK, the source code, or modified versions — free or
      paid — outside this project's official GitHub.
   c. Rename, re-logo, or rebrand it and distribute it as your own work
      (white-label), or remove this copyright and license notice.
   d. Use this app / code in or for any commercial product, service, or
      business activity.
   e. Use this app for spam, fraud, or anything that violates the law or
      WhatsApp's Terms of Service.

3. Third-party code
   Third-party components (including Baileys, nodejs-mobile, Node.js, pino,
   ws, esbuild, OkHttp, ZXing, AndroidX, Kotlin) remain under their own
   original licenses (MIT / Apache-2.0 / etc.). This license covers only the
   copyright holder's original work in this repository and does NOT restrict
   any rights granted by third-party licenses — including the GPL-3.0 of the
   bundled libsignal. See THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.md.

4. Contributions
   By submitting a pull request you agree it may be used and released in
   this project under this license.

5. No warranty
   THE SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED "AS IS", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND. This is an
   unofficial tool, not affiliated with WhatsApp / Meta or GitHub. You use it
   at your own risk (including your WhatsApp account being limited or
   banned). The copyright holder is not liable for any damages arising from
   the use of this software.

6. Termination
   The permissions in section 1 end automatically if you breach section 2.
   They are reinstated if the breach is cured within 30 days of notice.

7. Asking for permission
   Want to use it beyond what is allowed above (commercial use,
   redistribution, etc.)? Contact the copyright holder on GitHub:
   https://github.com/xykal

